      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the usual maximum for adults. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould this be a typo or a unit mix-up? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), the maximum immediate-release dose.\n- **500 mg three times daily** (1,500 mg/day), a common regimen.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is truly intended, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
